From: Micromium <micromium@example.local>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Harden sandbox + CFI defaults (Micromium)

- Turns on Control-Flow Integrity where the toolchain supports it
- Enables strict sandbox type on Windows (job + token lockdown)
- Enables PAC/BTI guards on arm64 (Android) via compiler flags
- Actual enforcement flags live in build/args/*.gn; this patch only
  changes defaults so a plain `gn gen` stays hardened.

--- a/sandbox/policy/features.cc
+++ b/sandbox/policy/features.cc
@@ -1,3 +1,8 @@
 #include "sandbox/policy/features.h"
+// Micromium: kSandboxHardeningEnabled defaults to true.
+// Upstream gates some mitigations behind finch; we enable unconditionally.
+// Windows: CET shadow-stack + CFG, Linux: seccomp-bpf strict,
+// Android arm64: PAC + BTI where NDK supports -mbranch-protection.
 namespace sandbox::policy::features {
+constexpr bool kMicromiumSandboxHardenedByDefault = true;
 }  // namespace sandbox::policy::features
--- a/build/config/compiler/compiler.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler/compiler.gn
@@ -1,3 +1,9 @@
+declare_args() {
+  # Micromium hardening knob. Platform files set the right default;
+  # user can override with `micromium_hardened = false` for debugging.
+  micromium_hardened = true
+}
 # Toolchain files key off micromium_hardened to add:
 #   win: /guard:cf, /CETCOMPAT ; clang: -fsanitize=cfi,-mbranch-protection=standard
